<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18239" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφέτ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφίημἰ</span>”
				<i>one who lets off a military engine,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					4.56.3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>teacher of ballistic,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				2.465.22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>c.</b>
			<i>starter</i> in races, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				152.1
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(vii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Astrol., <i>prorogator,</i> heavenly body which
			determines the vital quadrant, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Tetr.</u>
				131
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>a freed-slave</i> among the Spartans, <i><span class="en">
				Myro
				2
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
